        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> [@echasnovski](https://github.com/echasnovski) I like that idea, but wouldn't it be better to use `mini.snippets`? I'm not sure how to handle the letter count to adjust the frame. How would you do it?\n\nYeah, that's why it is not a good fit for 'mini.snippets' :) There might be a way through transfromations, but 'mini.snippets' doesn't support them.\n\nI don't know yet. The closest thing I have to this kind of feature is [pasting a \"section\"](https://github.com/echasnovski/nvim/blob/87961eb3956b3f12ce708ba7879764dccc398953/plugin/12_functions.lua#L75-L89) and starting Replace mode to enter the section title. But it is a bit different use case: fixed \"box\" and text overrides it.",
